Z||000000||sombre||02-07-2001||11:10 PM||||<BR>  Two quick questions...<P>  I in the process of re-doing the interior of my '86 SE V6.While I have the dash out I'm attempting to fix the delay wipers...They have not worked since I owned the car.Only come on once when you turn them to delay but they work fine on high or low,alsop they don't work with the washer.I remember reading something about the delay module under the dash but I can't find that post anymore,and I don't see anything in the harness near the column..Anybody have a decription and location for the dalay for the wipers???<P><BR>Second one is quick honest...I removed the sub amp(and the rest of the factory sub system)while I was at it I noticed another electronic box in the other side of the console(drivers side) under the carpet and plastic...anybody know what it is????<P>                       Thanx,<BR>                            Greg||||reg||5
Z||000001||DJRice||02-07-2001||11:37 PM||||The wiper delay module is mounted on the bottom of the dash to the right of the steering column.  It has a heatsink attached to it.  <P>The other box that you describe is your cruise control module.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||02-08-2001||09:14 AM||||uum under the carpet on the passengerside counsel.. thats the amp to the sub system. the cruise is vacuum actuated the ECM and vacuum control it.  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||02-08-2001||10:37 AM||||I have the entire interior of my 87 coupe taken apart.  I believe that when they changed ECMs from 86 to 87, they got rid of the cruise module and had it ECM controlled.  I too had a question about this, because my cruise is definatly vacuum/ecm controlled, but why do they illustrate the module in my 87 Helm manual?<P>------------------<BR>FieroJoe<BR>c311t@yahoo.com<BR>AIM: Fiero87311, Snowboarder0311<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||02-08-2001||07:17 PM||||The 1227748 ECM used for 87-88 4 cyl has the cruise built in. Without seeing the Helm drawing in question I can't tell you why it's in there.<P>Objects with heat sinks... just make sure don't confuse the delay unit for the dash lamp dimmer. The dimmer won't do you much good....<P>the wiper problem could be the delay module or the switch in the column. hard to say which one. ||||reg||1
Z||000005||sombre||02-08-2001||10:28 PM||||<BR>    How many plugs are on the delay???I seem to remeber something about a male and a female from the earlier post.think it said you could remove the module and plug them into each other and get just what I have.<P>   I'm only finding one gadget with a heat sink in my dash.It's about 2" square with 1 plug facing the front of the car.Is this the dimmer or the delay module???<P>  also anybody know if the wiper module is still available through GM???Or am I going to have to stand on my head at the local junkyard to find one???<P>   Thanks<BR>        Greg<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||sombre||02-12-2001||11:38 PM||||O.K. Just a little more help here.I think I found the plugs but no module...Going by the wire colors in a haynes manual I found a harness plug with the correct color/number of wires but it is pluged into a harness coming down out of the column right at the base of the column...I assume that the delay should have both of these plugged into it instead of each other....<P>   Anybody have a part # for the delay module????<P>                                Greg||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||02-13-2001||07:46 PM||||dimmer. about 2" square with one transistor on it. The socket is brown and covers one side of the heatsink. Has a single plug with 3 wire.<P>delay unit.... Not sure where it is exactly. haven't actually seen one I can remember. has 2 harness connectors I think. is larger than the dimmer.<P>You can likely get the delay unit from other GM cars. Stuff like that tends to be real common among models.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||sombre||02-13-2001||10:13 PM||||<BR>    Thanks for all the theories on the dimmer module.After talking to several knowledgeable people,acouple of parts stores and a pontiac parts manual.....<P><BR>     The location of the wiper delay control is on the board in the wiper motor housing...Fairly common thing in gm's I guess.board can be changed by itself but reatail id $79...So I'll be checking mine and then looking at the local bone yard for a replacement.<P>                        Thanx<BR>                            Greg||||reg||1
